    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d915">

                <pb facs="1208" n="1198" xml:id="pg1198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/12–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Freeman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-28">December 28,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received December 29—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. According to a notice published here today, conversion of puppet FRB notes
                    into CNC or <hi rendition="#italic">fapi</hi> in accordance with the 5 to 1 rate
                    will begin here at the Central Bank of China on January 4 and continue until
                    April 13th, after which date the FRB notes will become invalid.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d915-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking, repeated to Dept.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Freeman</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d915-f1" n="3" xml:id="d915-f1-content">
                <p>This information, differing somewhat in detail, was reported to the Department by
                    the Embassy in telegram No. 2055, November 28, 11 a.m. (893.51/11–2845).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
